  message: "Found while probing INV-zosun's untested neighbours, not while looking for it.\nMy first taint fixture used source_taint: secret_material and returned confirmed\nrc 0 — I read that as \"my fixture produces no flow\", which was half right and\nhalf the defect. Correcting the label to host_secret gave violated rc 1, so the\nfixture was fine and the label was the bug.\n\nDiscriminator: the boundary arm, given the same class of typo in the same\ncommand, exits 2 with a did-you-mean. One arm fails closed, the other fails\nopen, and the code comment justifying the closed one describes the open one.\n\nSeverity argument: this is cheaper to trip than any INV-zosun door. A\nmislabelled overlay takes deliberate effort; mistyping host_fs as\nhost_filesystem, or guessing secret_material for host_secret, is what an author\ndoes on a first attempt, with no vocabulary printed anywhere on the error path."  # c13c
